## Meet & Greet with AIG-Models Team

### Prateek Prabhanjan's team · [Hyperloom](https://github.com/AMD-AGI/Hyperloom)

**Their work:** Hyperloom — an agentic system that optimizes kernels on AMD HW.
GEAK is the kernel-optimizing part of Hyperloom (other parts create traces, etc.). Today GEAK runs on MI300.

**The two teams are two halves of one pipeline:**

```
┌─────────────────────┐     ┌─────────────────────┐     ┌─────────────────┐
│     AIG-Models      │     │        PAVS         │     │    Customers    │
├─────────────────────┤     ├─────────────────────┤     ├─────────────────┤
│ optimize the models │ ──► │ deploy on Edge HW   │ ──► │ edge deployment │
│ kernels,            │     │ GPK, NPU, GPU       │     │ on real robots  │
│ synthetic data      │     │ ROS, robot arm, AMR │     │                 │
└─────────────────────┘     └─────────────────────┘     └─────────────────┘
```

- **AIG-Models~(<span class="violet">AIG-M</span>)** optimize models — Kernel-Optimization, kernel generation, synthetic data Generation, Simulators.
- **PAVS** deployment of platforms & models — Edge HW (GPK, krk2e, PNR), PAI SDK, AMD-ROS, AMD-cUROBO, robot arm, AMR.

**Purpose of this deck:** the topics where the two teams overlap, and how we develop the collaboration.

---

<!-- _class: smallest -->

## Overlap Topics — and How We Develop Each

**1. Hyperloom → Edge HW**
Take the existing GEAK system (today on MI300) and extend it to GPK · krk2e · PNR; optimize models already in the PAI SDK on GPU + NPU through GEAK. Optimizing an NPU model is itself a step toward a NPU-Hyperloom. They can allocate an Engineer to help us On-board us to use GEAK. 
*<span style="color:#4caf50">Amol · Vaibhav · Karthik</span>*

**2. World Action Robotic Models**
<span class="violet">AIG-M</span> is developing & optimizing World Action models now (trending in the coming months). PAVS to understand, integrate, and benchmark them on Edge HW.
*<span style="color:#4caf50">Srini · Hari</span>*

**3. Synthetic Data Generation**
<span class="violet">AIG-M</span> has expertise in Genesis-style simulators. PAVS robotics / sim-to-real work can benefit from this.
*<span style="color:#4caf50">Ravi · Kush. Hari</span>*

**4. Kernel Generation**
<span class="violet">AIG-M</span> has proposed kernel-generation expertise. We can explore this to produce something like an MLIR optimization library (as in MIGraphX) on NPU. 

**<span style="color:#ff9800">5. Assets Exchange — schedule a robotics session</span>**
<span class="violet">AIG-M</span> wants to learn about PAVS assets: AMD-ROS pipelines and AMD-cUROBO motion planner. Set up a walkthrough with the robotics team; they were intested in working on some latest model development for edge deployment.

**<span style="color:#ff9800">6. Customer Gateway — HW access</span>**
<span class="violet">AIG-M</span> sees PAVS as their gateway to customers. They want to share our deployment HW (GPK board) to benchmark their models, and run them on our robotic arm and AMR, this would feedinto AIG-M's R&D. 
